Here are the limits of each function at $x=2$, according to the graphs:

$\begin{align}
&\blueD{\displaystyle\lim_{x\to 2}f(x)=0}
\\\\
&\maroonD{\displaystyle\lim_{x\to 2}g(x)=3}
\end{align}$

Now we can find $\displaystyle\lim_{x\to 2}\Big(f(x)-g(x)\Big)$ using the fact that the limit of a difference of functions is the difference of the individual limits:

$\displaystyle\lim_{x\to 2}\Big(f(x)-g(x)\Big)=\lim_{x\to 2}f(x)-\lim_{x\to 2}g(x)$
